---
// Policies: the index of every policy, with a short summary of each (src/lib/info.ts POLICIES).
// Two are written with the Code ↔ Paper reader, on another branch (/policies/code/,
// /policies/moderation/): linked once they exist, named until then.
import Info from "../../components/Info.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../../config";
import { pageExists, POLICIES } from "../../lib/info";
import { REVIEW_DAYS } from "../../lib/moderation";
---
<Info
  title="Policies"
  description={`${SITE_NAME}'s policies: licences and statements, the authors' code, the paper's full text, removals, moderation, DOIs, privacy, terms, conduct, accessibility, citation.`}
  group="policies"
  path="/policies/"
>
  <p class="lead" slot="lead">
    These are the rules {SITE_NAME} follows, one page per subject: what it shows and copies, what it does not do, how it
    decides on requests, and what it asks of the people who use it. Each page describes what the registry's code does,
    and says so when its rule changes.
  </p>

  <dl class="index">
    {POLICIES.map((l) => (
      <>
        <dt>{pageExists(l.href) ? <a href={l.href}>{l.text}</a> : <>{l.text} <span class="muted">(to be published)</span></>}</dt>
        <dd>{l.summary}</dd>
      </>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <h2 id="principles">The principles behind them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The paper and the repository are the reference. The registry records facts about them and links to them.</li>
    <li>Nothing is copied or reproduced beyond what its licence allows. When the licence of some code allows no copy, the
      reader's browser shows the file from its source, and the registry keeps no copy of it.</li>
    <li>No part of the registry asks for, shows or needs an email address.</li>
    <li>Published rules decide what people ask, and when in doubt they choose the safer outcome: hiding is automatic,
      and publishing needs a verified identity or checks that pass. The operator reviews what the rules cannot decide
      and can reverse what they did. No request waits more than {REVIEW_DAYS} days, except a request about personal
      data, which the operator answers within one month and does not close without an answer.</li>
    <li>Reading the registry is free, and the registry runs at no cost. It has no fees, no advertising and no
      tracking.</li>
  </ul>
</Info>
